        "id": 1000835
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-08-17T06:07:35Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Actually, thinking back to the time when we wrote the importer, I seem to recall that the importer always processed files in order. While File#list explicitly says that it provides no guarantees, this makes me think that something was already sorting the files before they reached this code, and thus sorting the list again here is not useful. \n\nDo we have evidence that these files are sometimes read in the wrong order?\n\nIt looks like pixel at least uses f2fs, could that be guaranteeing the order? If not, it might be something in Android itself.",
      "revId": "425ec7a92099817e0791dc26afca0f005efa8763",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "4eac75ea_e0df75e1",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1306837
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-08-18T02:48:21Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "1. Not in the field.\nWhen we adb push test files into the device.\nWe did observe the files are read in wrong order that causes NetworkStatsHistory#insertBuckets() take some time to move records.\n\n2. By looking into File#list(), it eventually calls readdir(), from man page the order depends on the filesystem. Which should be in common/fs/f2fs/dir.c\nhttps://osscs.corp.google.com/android/kernel/superproject/+/common-android-mainline:common/fs/f2fs/dir.c;l\u003d965;drc\u003d024aebcbf3e73cc03d86686719b43da1b7a83890;bpv\u003d1;bpt\u003d1\n\n+jaegeuk@ to input what is the order that f2fs list contents of a directory.",
      "parentUuid": "5157c4cc_660f54c1",
      "revId": "425ec7a92099817e0791dc26afca0f005efa8763",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "31d18d9d_ef12c289",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1176763
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-08-18T17:50:55Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Well, in general, f2fs does not guarantee in-order store/load, since it stores directory entries into multi-layer hash tables give hash(filename). However, we do store small # of directory entries in order, depending on # of files and it\u0027s length. So, how many files along with name lengths do you expect to store?",
      "parentUuid": "4eac75ea_e0df75e1",
      "revId": "425ec7a92099817e0791dc26afca0f005efa8763",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "18a94ccd_c441649f",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1306837
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-08-21T02:18:36Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Hi Jaegeuk,\n It\u0027s a directory with files with 10~500 KB. Files of each prefix are less than 6.\n\ne.g.\nhttps://paste.googleplex.com/5680939827986432",
      "parentUuid": "31d18d9d_ef12c289",
      "revId": "425ec7a92099817e0791dc26afca0f005efa8763",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c18e439f_48602f68",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1176763
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-08-21T19:11:00Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "In that case, I believe all the directory entries will be embedded in a single directory metadata. IOWs, they\u0027re sequentially stored and loaded.",
      "parentUuid": "18a94ccd_c441649f",
      "revId": "425ec7a92099817e0791dc26afca0f005efa8763",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "981aef71_8240c0ab",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1306837
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-08-22T02:31:29Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I see. Thanks for the feedback.\nHowever, IIRC I did see files were read in reverse order when local testing.\nIs there any case where the file are not listed in lexicographic order?\ne.g. store files in reverse order?\n\nHi Lorenzo,\n  For other possible future callers, as an improvement for FileRotator,\n  do we think it is good to merge this CL?",
      "parentUuid": "c18e439f_48602f68",
      "revId": "425ec7a92099817e0791dc26afca0f005efa8763",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "2eab2f69_94ff4e6d",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1176763
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-08-22T18:45:26Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "https://git.kernel.org/pub/scm/linux/kernel/git/jaegeuk/f2fs.git/tree/fs/f2fs/dir.c?h\u003ddev#n627\n\nThis finds the empty directory entry space when creating a file, which is in order. Could you please share how you\u0027re seeing the reverse order?",
      "parentUuid": "981aef71_8240c0ab",
      "revId": "425ec7a92099817e0791dc26afca0f005efa8763",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
